    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green. The suite that runs is the `AcceptanceTest` (both tests passing), and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **New helper** `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/OwnerSegment.java` \u2014 mirrors the existing `AgeBand`/`OwnerIdentityKey` helper style. `OwnerSegment.of(owner)` returns `'<TIER>_<AREA>'`:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when membershipLevel \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`. It uses the same null-guard the mapper already uses for `membershipLevel` (falls back to `MembershipLevels.of(owner)` when the transient field is unset).\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when the locality (from `Localities.localityOf(...)`) is a known region \u2014 NSW, VIC or QLD \u2014 else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` string `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` wiring `ownerSegment` to `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `STANDARD_METRO` for a Sydney (NSW) owner and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-region owner, each at membershipLevel 2 (STANDARD).",
